Below is a minimal example of a rotating card using only **HTML** and **CSS**.  
When you hover over the card it will rotate 180° around its Y‑axis (you can change the axis or angle if you wish).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D children */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y‑axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Optional: add front/back faces if you want a flip effect */
.card::before,
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

.card::before { /* Front face */
  background: #fff;
  z-index: 2;
}

.card::after { /* Back face */
  background: #f0f0f0;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  z-index: 1;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- You can put any content here -->
    <h2 style="margin:0;padding:20px;">Hello!</h2>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **`perspective`** on the wrapper gives the 3D space for the card to rotate in.
2. **`transform-style: preserve-3d`** keeps child elements in 3D space.
3. On hover, `transform: rotateY(180deg)` rotates the card.
4. The optional `::before` and `::after` pseudo‑elements let you create a front/back face if you want a flip effect.

Feel free to adjust the dimensions, colors, or rotation axis (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) to fit your design!
